# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE-391 working-tree additions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Editor / manual backups. These are pre-patch snapshots of main.py and ui.py
# kept so a manual rollback was possible during the refactor. They are 900 KB of
# duplicated source and nothing reads them; the git history is the rollback.
*.bak
main.py.bak
ui.py.bak
core/prompt - Copy.txt
core/*- Copy.txt

# Scratch tooling caches that appeared while driving the UI headlessly.
.playwright-mcp/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Partials from the model installers. A *.part means an install was interrupted
# and the licence/provenance sidecars were never written - committing one would
# ship a model with no licence record beside it.
*.part

# Live per-machine state. The app reads settings from %LOCALAPPDATA%\BrahmaAI,
# so this repo copy is a template only; anything that drifts into it by hand is
# ignored rather than trusted.
config/app_settings.local.json

# Node packages used only to vendor the VRM runtime (assets/avatar_vrm/vendor
# holds the copies that ARE committed, with their licences).
node_modules/
package-lock.json
package.json

# Live2D Cubism runtime, generated by scripts/setup_live2d_cubism.ps1. Unlike
# the VRM runtime, this is ~800 KB of esbuild output plus a downloaded Core, all
# regenerable from pinned upstream commits - so it is built on demand rather
# than committed. index.html is the tracked source of truth.
assets/avatar_live2d/vendor/
